-- title:
--   Cohomologous tangent cocycles give isomorphic regluings
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and commutative rings $B$, $B_1$, with $B$ local and artinian and with algebraically closed residue field, and $B_1$ a $B$-algebra. The hypotheses on the base are: `hπ`, the structure map $B \to B_1$ is surjective; `hker`, its kernel $I = \ker(B \to B_1)$ is nilpotent; `hsmall`, $I \cdot \mathfrak m_B = 0$, so that $B \to B_1$ is a small extension; `hq`, the image of $q$ in $B$ is nilpotent; and `hI`, $I \subseteq \mathfrak m_B$.
--
--   Over $B_1$ there are given a scheme $A_1$, a morphism $f_1 : A_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} B_1$, a relative group law $L_1$ on $f_1$ (functorial multiplication, unit, inverse on points of $f_1$ over varying $B_1$-schemes, with associativity, unit and inverse laws and naturality), the hypothesis `hc₁` that $L_1$ is commutative, and `h₁`, an `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle` for $f_1$: $f_1$ is smooth and proper, its fibres are connected, and it admits a relative group law. Formal data along the unit section are given as well: a commutative formal group law $F$ in two variables over $B$; formal coordinates $\theta_1$ for $f_1$ of dimension $2$, that is, an assignment to each $B_1$-algebra $B'$ and each tuple $s \in (B')^2$ of a point of $f_1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} B'$; and `hθ₁`, the assertion that $\theta_1$ are formal coordinates for $L_1$ with respect to the base change $F \otimes_B B_1$, i.e. compatibility with $B_1$-algebra maps on nilpotent tuples together with, for every ideal $J$ with $J^{n+1} = 0$, the statements that $J$-valued tuples give $J$-infinitesimal points, that $\theta_1$ is injective on $J$-valued tuples, that every $J$-infinitesimal point of $f_1$ is of this form, and that the truncated formal multiplication $F.\mathrm{nilMul}$ corresponds to the multiplication of $L_1$. Two further conditions on this data are imposed: `hinf₁`, for every $B_1$-algebra $C$, every $m$ and every point $P$ of $f_1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $q^m P$ equal to the unit, there is a nilpotent ideal $J \subseteq C$ such that $P$ is $J$-infinitesimal for $L_1$; and `hheight`, for every field $k$ and every surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to k$, the quotient of $k[[x_1,x_2]]$ by the ideal generated by the components of the $q$-th iterated series $(F \otimes_\rho k).\mathrm{nthSeries}\, q$ has $k$-dimension $q^4$.
--
--   The tangent module is a $\operatorname{ResidueField} B$-vector space $V$, finite-dimensional, carrying also a compatible $B$-module structure and a central right action of the residue field, together with an injective $B$-linear map $\iota : V \to B$ whose range is $I$ viewed as a $B$-submodule (`hι`, `hιI`).
--
--   The deformation being reglued is $D_0$, a bare deformation of $(f_1, L_1)$ over $B$: a scheme $D_0.A$ with a morphism $D_0.f$ to $\operatorname{Spec} B$, assumed separated, a commutative relative group law $D_0.L$, an `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle` for $D_0.f$, and a morphism $D_0.g : A_1 \to D_0.A$ making the square over $\operatorname{Spec} B_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ cartesian and compatible with the multiplications. Further there are an ordered affine open cover $\mathcal U$ of $D_0.A$ (a finite linearly ordered family of affine opens covering $D_0.A$), a distinguished index $i_0$, a morphism $e_0 : \operatorname{Spec} B \to \mathcal U.U\, i_0$ with `he₀`: $e_0$ followed by the inclusion $(\mathcal U.U\, i_0).\iota$ is the unit section of $D_0.L$ over $\operatorname{Spec} B$, and, on the special fibre, a morphism $e_1 : \operatorname{Spec}(\operatorname{ResidueField} B) \to (\mathcal U.\mathrm{baseChange}\, D_0.f\, (\operatorname{ResidueField} B)).U\, i_0$ with `he₁`: $e_1$ followed by the inclusion of that chart is the unit section of the base change of $D_0.L$ along $\operatorname{Spec}(\operatorname{ResidueField} B) \to \operatorname{Spec} B$; here the base-changed cover is the preimage of $\mathcal U$ under the first projection of $\mathrm{pullback}\, D_0.f\, (\mathrm{specMap}\, B\, (\operatorname{ResidueField} B))$. A comparison datum on overlaps is given by a family $\sigma$ of ring isomorphisms
--   $$\operatorname{ResidueField} B \otimes_B \Gamma(D_0.A, \mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\, s) \;\cong\; \Gamma\bigl(\mathrm{pullback}\, D_0.f\, (\mathrm{specMap}\, B\, (\operatorname{ResidueField} B)),\ (\mathcal U.\mathrm{baseChange}\, D_0.f\, (\operatorname{ResidueField} B)).\mathrm{inter}\, s\bigr)$$
--   indexed by $s \in \mathcal U.\mathrm{Idx}\, 1$, i.e. by strictly increasing pairs of indices, $\mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\, s$ being the intersection of the corresponding two charts; the $B$-algebra structure on the sections is the one induced by $D_0.f$. Two normalisations are imposed: `hσ₁`, $\sigma_s(1 \otimes x)$ is the restriction to the base-changed intersection of the image of $x$ under the comparison map of the first projection on $\mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\, s$; and `hσ₂`, $\sigma_s(a \otimes 1)$ is the image of $a$ under the structure map of the residue field into those sections, via the second projection.
--
--   The cocycles are two elements $c, c'$ of the space of point derivations $\mathrm{Algebra.PointDerivations}$ of $\Gamma$ of the pullback on the chart $U\, i_0$ of the base-changed cover, at the evaluation homomorphism to $\operatorname{ResidueField} B$ determined by $e_1$, with values in the space of $\operatorname{ResidueField} B$-linear maps from the dual $V^\vee$ to the Čech $1$-cochains of the presheaf $\mathrm{OModulePresheaf.unit}$ of the second projection with respect to the base-changed cover; a point derivation at $\mathrm{ev}$ is a linear map $D$ with $D(ab) = \mathrm{ev}(a)\,D(b) + \mathrm{ev}(b)\,D(a)$, and the $1$-cochains are families indexed by the strictly increasing pairs $s$ of sections over $\mathrm{inter}\, s$. The hypotheses `hc` and `hc'` state that for every section $a$ and every $\xi \in V^\vee$ the cochains $c(a)(\xi)$ and $c'(a)(\xi)$ lie in the kernel of the Čech differential $d^1$, i.e. are $1$-cocycles.
--
--   The regluing data are two families $\tau, \tau'$ of automorphisms $\tau_s, \tau'_s$ of the schemes $\mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\, s$, and two bare deformations $D, D'$ of $(f_1, L_1)$ over $B$ with `hD`: $D_0.\mathrm{IsRegluingBy}\ \mathcal U\ \tau\ D$, and `hD'`: the same for $\tau'$ and $D'$. The predicate $\mathrm{IsRegluingBy}$ asserts that each $\tau_s$ is a morphism over $D_0.f$, that it fixes the restriction of $D_0.g$ to $\mathrm{inter}\, s$, and that there exists a family of open immersions $\mathcal U.U\, i \to D.A$ over $D_0.f$, jointly surjective on points, compatible with $D_0.g$, and satisfying on each overlap $\mathrm{inter}\, s$ that the inclusion into the chart of smaller index followed by its immersion equals $\tau_s$ followed by the inclusion into the chart of larger index followed by its immersion.
--
--   The link between $\tau$, $\tau'$ and $c$, $c'$ is `hτ`, respectively `hτ'`: for each strictly increasing pair $s$ there exists a map
--   $$c_s : \Gamma(\mathrm{pullback}\ \ldots, (\mathcal U.\mathrm{baseChange}\ \ldots).U\, i_0) \longrightarrow \bigl(V^\vee \to_{\operatorname{ResidueField} B} \operatorname{ResidueField} B \otimes_B \Gamma(D_0.A, \mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\, s)\bigr)$$
--   such that, first, $\mathrm{IsTangentCoordsOfPairAt}$ holds for the ideal $I$, the module $V$, the map $\iota$, the ring $\Gamma(D_0.A, \mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\, s)$, the pair of morphisms given by the canonical $\mathrm{fromSpec}$ of the affine open $\mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\, s$ and by $\mathrm{isoSpec}^{-1}$ followed by $\tau_s$ (respectively $\tau'_s$) followed by the inclusion into $D_0.A$, the second projection of the pullback with its base-changed group law, the first projection, the chart $U\, i_0$ of the base-changed cover, and $c_s$; unfolded, this says that there are a morphism $w_0$ from the spectrum of the thickening $(\operatorname{ResidueField} B \otimes_B \Gamma(D_0.A, \mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\, s)) \otimes_{\operatorname{ResidueField} B} \mathrm{TrivSqZeroExt}(\operatorname{ResidueField} B, V)$ to the special fibre lying over the square-zero base, and a lift $w_1$ to the chart of the group-law translate of $w_0$, such that the composite of $w_0$ with the first projection is tangent to the given pair of morphisms in the sense of $\mathrm{IsTangentOfPair}$, and $c_s$ equals the tangent coordinates of the chart ring homomorphism attached to $w_1$. Second, $\sigma_s(c_s(a)(\xi))$ equals the component at $s$ of $c(a)(\xi)$ (respectively of $c'(a)(\xi)$) for all $a$ and all $\xi \in V^\vee$.
--
--   The final hypothesis `hcob` is the coboundary condition: for every section $a$ over the chart $U\, i_0$ of the base-changed cover and every $\xi \in V^\vee$ there exists a Čech $0$-cochain $b$ of $\mathrm{OModulePresheaf.unit}$ for the base-changed cover with $d^0 b = c(a)(\xi) - c'(a)(\xi)$.
--
--   The conclusion is $D.\mathrm{IsIso}\, D'$: there exists an isomorphism of schemes $e : D.A \cong D'.A$ such that $e$ followed by $D'.f$ equals $D.f$, and $D.g$ followed by $e$ equals $D'.g$.
--
--   This is the converse direction of the cocycle description of regluings of a bare deformation across a small extension: two regluings whose tangent cocycles differ, componentwise, by a Čech coboundary are isomorphic as deformations over $B$, compatibly with the comparison morphisms from $A_1$. It is obtained by assembling the coboundary into chart automorphisms and feeding these into the chartwise criterion [`GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.isIso_of_isRegluingBy_of_forall_comp_hom_eq`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.isIso_of_isRegluingBy_of_forall_comp_hom_eq), and it is used in [`GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.isShiftBy_of_isShiftBy_of_isRegluingBy_of_exists_d_eq_sub`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.isShiftBy_of_isShiftBy_of_isRegluingBy_of_exists_d_eq_sub).
